WEBVTT

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:05.940
<b>1939    Europe</b>

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.240
<i>1939.</i>

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:13.190
<i>Humanity was faced with the sudden 
appearance of a mysterious foe.</i>

00:00:13.630 --> 00:00:16.330
<i>They called it the Neuroi.</i>

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:33.090
<i>In the blink of an eye,</i>

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:36.390
<i>the Neuroi successfully invaded most of Europe,</i>

00:00:36.390 --> 00:00:39.550
<i>stealing many people's homes and nations.</i>

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:49.240
<i>To combat the Neuroi, 
humanity developed a new weapon,</i>

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:54.510
<i>the flying Striker Units that could 
only be used by Witches,</i>

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:56.530
<i>girls with magical power.</i>

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:03.150
<i>Witches across the world gathered to use 
these Striker Units against the Neuroi.</i>

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.050
<i>A unit of these Witches was formed.</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.430
<i>The Allied Forces' 502nd Joint Fighter Wing.</i>

00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:17.650
<i>People called them the "Brave Witches."</i>

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.960
<b>Episode 1
"The Witch of Sasebo?"</b>

00:03:18.260 --> 00:03:21.260
<b>1944    September</b>

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:24.220
<b>Fusou Empire    Sasebo</b>

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:53.420
<b>Fusou Imperial Navy    Hario Transceiver Station</b>

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:53.410
Good morning!

00:03:54.510 --> 00:03:55.550
Dad!

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:57.780
Here's your lunch.

00:03:57.780 --> 00:03:59.830
Oh, thanks.

00:03:59.830 --> 00:04:01.970
Well? Did you fix the receiver?

00:04:01.970 --> 00:04:04.590
Yeah, he had it fixed in a jiffy.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:05.530
Great!

00:04:05.530 --> 00:04:06.840
That's my dad for you!

00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:10.310
No telling when we might get 
an important message...

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:12.350
Engineer Karibuchi is our savior.

00:04:12.610 --> 00:04:16.690
This transceiver station can reach all the 
way to South Sea Island, can't it?

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:19.900
Yes, it's Fusou's tallest radio tower.

00:04:19.900 --> 00:04:21.650
Wow!

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.560
Sub-lieutenant Mizunuma, a message.

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:24.880
A message?

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:27.820
I see.

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.810
The Third Carrier Division will 
arrive in port this afternoon.

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:32.780
The Third Carrier Division?

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:34.030
That's my big sis!

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:38.490
Yeah, Sub-lieutenant Karibuchi Takami, 
the hero of Sasebo, is returning home.

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:40.160
All right!

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:44.710
<i>My big sis is coming back.</i>

00:04:48.500 --> 00:04:50.610
<i>I feel like I can pull it off today.</i>

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:04.770
One!

00:05:06.330 --> 00:05:07.070
Two!

00:05:09.520 --> 00:05:10.150
Three—

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:17.910
I'm back!

00:05:17.910 --> 00:05:19.110
Oh, my...

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:21.330
Couldn't quite make it across again today?

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:24.350
Forget that! They say Sis 
is coming back today!

00:05:24.350 --> 00:05:25.540
Takami?

00:05:25.540 --> 00:05:27.590
Things are always so sudden with that girl.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.140
Because of her mission. She can't help it.

00:05:31.510 --> 00:05:33.230
See you later!

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:34.690
Wait! You aren't changing?

00:05:34.690 --> 00:05:36.010
It'll dry as I run!

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.270
<b>Sasebo Aviation Preparatory School</b>

00:05:42.670 --> 00:05:44.170
Next! Akiyama!

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:44.690
Right.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.410
Your body isn't keeping pace with the engine!

00:05:59.410 --> 00:06:00.810
Ten laps around the courtyard!

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.050
Next! Watanabe!

00:06:02.050 --> 00:06:02.510
Right.

00:06:04.600 --> 00:06:07.110
I heard Sub-lieutenant Karibuchi is returning.

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.260
Yeah, from Allied Naval Training.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:10.600
It's been three months.

00:06:10.600 --> 00:06:11.890
She's so amazing.

00:06:11.890 --> 00:06:14.540
I can't believe they assigned 
her to a carrier division!

00:06:15.550 --> 00:06:16.630
Oh, yeah...

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:20.770
The next movie they're producing is based 
on her time in Europe, isn't it?

00:06:20.890 --> 00:06:21.900
That's right!

00:06:21.900 --> 00:06:25.860
She held off the enemy forces alone 
during the retreat from Libau!

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:28.330
She really is the hero of Sasebo!

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:34.820
Sub-lieutenant Karibuchi must be really sad 
to have a failure of a sister like you.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:36.050
Misumi-san...

00:06:36.050 --> 00:06:37.930
What? What does that mean?!

00:06:38.380 --> 00:06:39.790
Just what I said.

00:06:39.790 --> 00:06:41.250
Next! Misumi!

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:42.140
Right.

00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:47.650
Don't let her get to you, Hikari.

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:48.710
Yeah.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.770
A corkscrew maneuver!

00:06:52.770 --> 00:06:54.430
That's an upperclassman's maneuver!

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:57.350
All right!

00:07:00.950 --> 00:07:02.470
Next! Karibuchi!

00:07:02.470 --> 00:07:03.010
Right.

00:07:05.360 --> 00:07:06.390
<i>I can do that, too!</i>

00:07:10.790 --> 00:07:11.740
She's spinning?

00:07:14.990 --> 00:07:15.730
Hikari!

00:07:18.340 --> 00:07:19.690
Ow...

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:20.990
Are you stupid?!

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:23.490
What moron falls from a 
sky without enemies?!

00:07:23.810 --> 00:07:25.290
Give me twenty laps!

00:07:25.830 --> 00:07:26.710
Right!

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:27.630
Pathetic.

00:07:28.730 --> 00:07:32.000
I can't believe you're the little 
sister of Karibuchi Takami,

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:33.290
the hero of Sasebo.

00:07:33.340 --> 00:07:35.370
You get Fs for grades.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:37.800
Do you really think you can join a Witch unit?

00:07:37.800 --> 00:07:40.300
I do! Is that wrong?

00:07:40.780 --> 00:07:42.980
I'm going to be a Witch, like my sister!

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:45.730
You're an overly optimistic idiot.

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:49.580
Next! Kobayashi!

00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:50.480
Right.

00:07:50.490 --> 00:07:52.740
<b>Principal    Kitagou Fumika</b>

00:07:54.590 --> 00:07:55.860
Bye!

00:07:55.870 --> 00:07:57.440
She's running again.

00:07:57.440 --> 00:07:59.250
She has the most stamina 
out of the whole school.

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.690
If only her magic power were that strong...

00:08:08.420 --> 00:08:10.300
<b>The Wings of Libau</b>

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:28.140
Big sis!

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.980
Big sis!

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.820
Hey! Hey—

00:08:44.270 --> 00:08:46.070
I'm back, Hikari.

00:08:46.070 --> 00:08:48.070
Welcome back, Sis!

00:08:52.170 --> 00:08:53.830
Takami-chan's late.

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:56.840
I want to hear her talk about Libau again...

00:08:57.130 --> 00:08:57.960
There she is.

00:08:58.810 --> 00:09:00.480
What a nice car!

00:09:00.480 --> 00:09:03.210
Well, she is the hero of Sasebo.

00:09:06.230 --> 00:09:07.540
Hikari!

00:09:08.550 --> 00:09:10.020
I'm back...

00:09:11.620 --> 00:09:13.180
I'm home.

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:16.690
That's Takami-chan for you!

00:09:18.820 --> 00:09:21.250
Sorry for all the fuss.

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:22.740
I'm sure you want to relax.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.820
No, it's easier for me to relax like this.

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.160
Look at this, Sis!

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.670
<b>The Hero of Libau</b>

00:09:27.490 --> 00:09:28.340
Ta-dah!

00:09:28.340 --> 00:09:29.660
They're articles about you!

00:09:30.190 --> 00:09:31.950
She saved them all.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:35.530
That's embarrassing...

00:09:35.530 --> 00:09:37.200
No, it isn't.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:40.560
It's proof that you're doing 
a great job as a Witch

00:09:40.560 --> 00:09:43.300
Oh, right! I have to check today's paper.

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:45.060
An article on Witches!

00:09:45.600 --> 00:09:50.060
"Lieutenant Commander Sakamoto
fights hard as a member

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:54.660
of the 501st Joint Fighter Wing, 
the Strike Witches."

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:57.680
Sis, do you know Lieutenant 
Commander Sakamoto?

00:09:57.680 --> 00:10:00.190
I was with her during the retreat from Libau.

00:10:00.530 --> 00:10:03.740
She was tough, but someone 
you could really respect.

00:10:08.050 --> 00:10:10.250
Is she a Fusou Witch, too?

00:10:10.250 --> 00:10:12.000
I don't know...

00:10:12.000 --> 00:10:16.000
If a Fusou Witch were deployed 
to a Joint Fighter Wing,

00:10:16.000 --> 00:10:18.370
it should have made the news...

00:10:22.910 --> 00:10:25.620
It's been so long since I could relax in a bath!

00:10:26.040 --> 00:10:28.420
Water is precious on a ship, right?

00:10:28.420 --> 00:10:29.560
Yes.

00:10:29.950 --> 00:10:32.010
Hey, Sis, show it to me...

00:10:33.100 --> 00:10:34.340
Again?

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:40.780
Is it that fun to look at a scar?

00:10:41.110 --> 00:10:45.630
But you got that scar fighting to protect 
everyone during the Libau retreat, right?

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:47.210
It's so cool!

00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:50.380
That tickles!

00:10:51.350 --> 00:10:52.740
Oh, yeah, Sis.

00:10:52.740 --> 00:10:55.250
A new parlor opened near the station!

00:10:55.450 --> 00:10:59.660
Your expedition's over, so you'll be 
in Sasebo for a while, won't you?

00:11:00.730 --> 00:11:01.730
What's wrong?

00:11:02.060 --> 00:11:03.670
Actually, Hikari,

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:07.390
when I got to port today, 
I received new orders.

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:08.720
Orders?

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:13.720
I'm being deployed to Europe.

00:11:16.350 --> 00:11:17.540
Europe?

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:22.990
<b>Witch

00:11:32.600 --> 00:11:34.160
Good morning, Mom.

00:11:35.030 --> 00:11:36.000
Morning.

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:36.830
Where's Hikari?

00:11:45.590 --> 00:11:49.680
I'm being deployed to Europe.

00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:53.660
<i>Sis is going away again.</i>

00:11:55.380 --> 00:11:56.370
Hikari!

00:11:59.170 --> 00:11:59.830
Sis!

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:11.040
Try leaping off the air, before you 
feel the water on your feet.

00:12:20.500 --> 00:12:21.600
Hikari?

00:12:24.190 --> 00:12:25.890
That was close...

00:12:32.060 --> 00:12:33.560
Everyone...

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:37.820
As you know, the situation in Europe is grim.

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:41.230
They need more Witches, 
and they need them now.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:47.230
Thus, our school will take a volunteer 
for deployment to Europe.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.960
Deployment to Europe?

00:12:49.960 --> 00:12:54.000
Since you will be a student, you won't 
be deployed to the far front lines.

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:56.460
But the mission won't be easy.

00:12:56.460 --> 00:12:58.130
If you're interested, raise your hand.

00:13:01.400 --> 00:13:04.350
You're the head of the first-year class...

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:06.460
Misumi Miya.

00:13:06.460 --> 00:13:09.980
I'm only a first-year student, but I 
believe my skill will more than suffice.

00:13:11.390 --> 00:13:12.980
I volunteer, too!

00:13:13.880 --> 00:13:16.230
First-year Karibuchi Hikari!

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:18.100
You?

00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:20.360
I want to go to Europe, too!

00:13:21.540 --> 00:13:22.710
Very well.

00:13:22.710 --> 00:13:26.990
In three days, we'll hold a selection 
exam to see who is best qualified.

00:13:28.860 --> 00:13:30.380
A selection exam?

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:31.290
That's right.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:34.610
If I beat Misumi-san there,
I can go to Europe!

00:13:35.010 --> 00:13:38.110
But are they that desperate for Witches?

00:13:38.110 --> 00:13:41.250
You aren't even out of school yet.

00:13:41.630 --> 00:13:46.050
Even Takami waited until she was out 
of school to join the military.

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:49.210
But by my age, she'd graduated!

00:13:49.210 --> 00:13:51.500
Because she was given special promotions.

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:56.410
Aren't you always telling me a Witch 
should strive to serve others?

00:13:56.410 --> 00:13:58.380
Why can't I go?!

00:13:59.050 --> 00:14:01.220
I'm a Witch, too!

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:03.300
Hikari...

00:14:05.090 --> 00:14:06.870
Wait, you two!

00:14:17.690 --> 00:14:18.590
Hikari...

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:24.840
Every day, I've been running the 
same course that you ran.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:26.940
I've been doing the same training.

00:14:27.910 --> 00:14:30.350
I thought if I could cross the sea like you,

00:14:30.350 --> 00:14:32.600
maybe I could catch up to you.

00:14:33.530 --> 00:14:35.730
If I flunk the exam, I'll give up.

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:39.630
A weak Witch in Europe will just 
cause problems for everyone.

00:14:40.120 --> 00:14:43.350
But I don't want to give up 
without doing anything!

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:48.290
Sure, good luck, Hikari.

00:14:51.760 --> 00:14:55.100
We will now begin the exam to 
determine who goes to Europe.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:57.860
The exam is modeled on an actual battle.

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.840
Both participants will be given weapons

00:14:59.840 --> 00:15:03.370
and asked to complete tasks 
within the allotted time.

00:15:04.670 --> 00:15:06.710
If you can't pass through the checkpoints

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:09.250
or clear the exam in time, you will fail.

00:15:10.160 --> 00:15:12.030
If both participants pass,

00:15:12.030 --> 00:15:14.770
the faster one will be chosen for deployment.

00:15:19.630 --> 00:15:20.510
Ready!

00:15:34.820 --> 00:15:36.550
I don't like those clouds.

00:15:36.870 --> 00:15:39.530
European skies aren't exactly gentle.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:41.630
That's true.

00:15:43.460 --> 00:15:44.810
This exam's a waste of time.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:48.740
There's no way you can 
beat me, and you know it!

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:51.050
We won't know that until we try!

00:15:51.250 --> 00:15:53.830
Then, I'll make you understand!

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:09.570
Not even close.

00:16:18.500 --> 00:16:20.680
Two Witches are approaching.

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:25.330
<b>Third Carrier Division Admiral
Oosawa Yoshizaburo</b>

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:25.330
<b>Fusou Imperial Navy
Lt Commander Shindou Mie</b>

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:26.970
Admiral, is there any point in sending 
an inexperienced student to Europe?

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:30.660
We can't ignore Europe's demands.

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:33.440
There's no telling when our country 
will become a war zone.

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:38.520
And you also started as a beginner, 
didn't you Shindou-kun?

00:16:40.510 --> 00:16:41.430
They're here.

00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:02.700
She's moving pretty well.

00:17:14.480 --> 00:17:17.210
Is that Sub-lieutenant Karibuchi's 
younger sister?

00:17:17.210 --> 00:17:18.030
Yes.

00:17:20.320 --> 00:17:21.940
It's going to storm.

00:17:22.400 --> 00:17:25.170
The enemy won't always fight 
when we want them to.

00:17:29.560 --> 00:17:31.280
The rain is getting in my eyes...

00:17:31.720 --> 00:17:33.200
My clothes are heavy!

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.550
She's getting closer?

00:17:46.880 --> 00:17:49.430
She isn't dropping her speed in this weather?

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:51.090
How does she have so much stamina?

00:17:58.190 --> 00:18:00.420
Almost... Almost!

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:04.660
If I don't decrease the magical power 
I'm using, she'll catch up.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:09.200
I need to get closer to the water's 
surface and build some lift!

00:18:13.200 --> 00:18:14.910
Just one more checkpoint!

00:18:15.290 --> 00:18:16.630
She pulled away again.

00:18:17.200 --> 00:18:18.520
At this rate...

00:18:19.370 --> 00:18:20.340
Watch out!

00:18:31.260 --> 00:18:33.220
Message from the final checkpoint.

00:18:33.480 --> 00:18:36.460
Neither Misumi nor Karibuchi arrived.

00:18:36.460 --> 00:18:37.600
What?

00:18:43.080 --> 00:18:43.980
Misumi-san!

00:18:49.350 --> 00:18:50.540
Misumi-san!

00:18:51.110 --> 00:18:52.710
Misumi-san!

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:55.660
Karibuchi-san...

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:04.620
One!

00:19:06.030 --> 00:19:06.820
Two!

00:19:12.900 --> 00:19:13.920
Three!

00:19:22.080 --> 00:19:23.550
Karibuchi...

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:27.420
Ow...

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:29.390
Misumi-san!

00:19:30.320 --> 00:19:31.450
Misumi-san!

00:19:35.880 --> 00:19:37.610
I'm so glad.

00:19:38.640 --> 00:19:39.920
Karibuchi-san...

00:19:40.520 --> 00:19:43.290
Thank you for saving me.

00:19:44.190 --> 00:19:45.850
I didn't...

00:19:49.600 --> 00:19:53.170
I... I crossed the sea.

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:54.930
I did it.

00:19:55.200 --> 00:19:56.850
I did it!

00:19:56.850 --> 00:19:58.510
I did it, Misumi-san!

00:19:58.880 --> 00:20:00.280
Thank you!

00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:01.550
What?

00:20:02.350 --> 00:20:04.510
She managed to cross that sea?

00:20:07.820 --> 00:20:12.500
<i>Since neither of us made it back in time,</i>

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:14.100
<i>we both failed the exam.</i>

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.640
You seem kind of happy, Hikari...

00:20:26.350 --> 00:20:28.260
I failed the exam,

00:20:28.260 --> 00:20:31.550
but I feel I've grown a little closer to you.

00:20:32.190 --> 00:20:37.440
I'm going to work even harder, 
so I can fly with you!

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:38.560
Yeah.

00:20:38.820 --> 00:20:39.800
I'll be waiting!

00:20:44.810 --> 00:20:46.910
Good morning!

00:20:47.270 --> 00:20:49.100
The sub-lieutenant's with you today?

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.260
Good morning.

00:20:51.360 --> 00:20:53.720
Here's your lunch, Dad.

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:55.310
Oh, thanks.

00:20:56.200 --> 00:20:57.810
Incoming message, Sub-lieutenant.

00:21:01.570 --> 00:21:02.810
It's for Hikari-chan.

00:21:03.710 --> 00:21:04.560
For me?

00:21:07.140 --> 00:21:08.840
It's from the Navy General Staff.

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:13.430
"Karibuchi Hikari has passed her exam.

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:16.330
Prepare for deployment to Europe."

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.030
Is this...

00:21:18.030 --> 00:21:19.360
You did it, Hikari!

00:21:19.360 --> 00:21:22.080
You passed! We can go 
to Europe together!

00:21:25.800 --> 00:21:27.210
Passed...

00:21:28.150 --> 00:21:29.660
I passed?

00:21:32.390 --> 00:21:34.330
It's because you worked so hard.

00:21:35.870 --> 00:21:38.030
I did it! I did it!

00:21:38.030 --> 00:21:39.950
I did it!

00:21:42.550 --> 00:21:48.960
<i>At the same time, a new Neuroi nest 
was being established in Europe.</i>

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:54.940
<b>To Be Continued</b>

00:23:25.990 --> 00:23:30.130
With much expectation and hope in our 
hearts, Sis and I head to Europe.

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:32.110
But suddenly the Neuroi attack.

00:23:32.110 --> 00:23:34.800
Wait, Sis! I'll fight with you!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:38.490
Next time, on <i>Brave Witches</i>: 
Take Flight, Chidori

00:23:38.600 --> 00:23:39.970
<b>Episode 2
"Take Flight, Chidori."</b>

00:23:39.970 --> 00:23:41.970
<b></b>
